2
00:00:03,254 --> 00:00:07,172
اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:09,507 --> 00:00:10,868
Chapter Nine: On Dueling,

4
00:00:12,753 --> 00:00:14,722
translating Mubariza(مُبَارزَة), as dueling,

5
00:00:14,991 --> 00:00:19,031
which is pretty much the closest translation you can get for the word Mubariza(مُبَارزَة),

6
00:00:20,882 --> 00:00:27,686
the way it(Dueling) used to happen in the old days is that, this(Dueling) is before the actual battle starts.

7
00:00:30,387 --> 00:00:33,879
Someone who is well known with a reputation of being good fighter,

8
00:00:34,364 --> 00:00:40,699
he would come ahead before the battle starts, while the armies are still meeting,

9
00:00:41,119 --> 00:00:45,390
and would ask for a challenge for one man to come out and challenge him.

10
00:00:45,881 --> 00:00:52,286
This is sort of like the ceremony to open the celebration of the actual battle.

11
00:00:53,905 --> 00:00:58,494
And we know what happened in the Battle of Badr(بدر), in fact Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) does talk about that,

12
00:00:59,177 --> 00:01:03,288
where three of the Mushrikeen(مشركين) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

13
00:01:03,336 --> 00:01:10,640
Ut'ba Bin Rabiyah(عُتْبَة بن ربيعة), Shaibah(شيبة) and Al-Walid Bin Ut'ba(ألوليدبن عُتْبَة) three of them set out for Mubariza(مُبَارزَة).

14
00:01:12,590 --> 00:01:17,383
And this also existed even in the era of firearms.

15
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:20,903
Where, you had the duels in the wild, wild west,

16
00:01:21,728 --> 00:01:27,878
where people will do those 10 steps and then you turn around and shoot your opponent,

17
00:01:27,918 --> 00:01:31,124
stuff that is not only in the movies, it's absolutely bad that happened.

18
00:01:31,164 --> 00:01:38,809
One of the US presidents was or president candidate was killed in a duel.

19
00:01:41,093 --> 00:01:47,434
So Mubariza(مُبَارزَة) is something that carried on until quite recently.

20
00:01:50,083 --> 00:01:52,947
Dueling is allowed according to the consensus of the scholars,

21
00:01:53,954 --> 00:01:57,309
accepting the invitation to duel by an non-believers is recommended.

22
00:01:58,208 --> 00:02:03,345
Asking for a duel is neither recommended nor discouraged, according to the Maz'hab(مذهب) of As-Shafie(ألشَّافعي),

23
00:02:04,258 --> 00:02:11,126
it is appropriate for the experienced, and is discouraged for the weak, doesn't have sufficient confidence in himself.

24
00:02:12,412 --> 00:02:21,113
You don't went to go out, bravado and just ask for duel, when you don't have the ability to stand up to the opponent.

25
00:02:21,195 --> 00:02:23,336
Why? Because that demoralizes the army.

26
00:02:24,257 --> 00:02:27,117
The Mubariza(مُبَارزَة) that happened before the Battle of Badr(بدر),

27
00:02:27,283 --> 00:02:32,199
played a very important role in demoralizing the army of the disbelievers

28
00:02:32,262 --> 00:02:35,841
because all of their three men who came up with Mubariza(مُبَارزَة) were killed.

29
00:02:38,603 --> 00:02:42,346
So it is Makroh(مكروع) for the one, who is not capable.

30
00:02:43,751 --> 00:02:47,896
In fact, it is said that it is prohibited for such a person to ask for duel,

31
00:02:49,079 --> 00:02:53,539
it is Sunnah(سنة) get the permission of the Ameer(أمير), but it is still allowed without his knowledge,

32
00:02:54,079 --> 00:02:59,964
because duels don't only happen before the battle, but within the battle you could call on somebody, you see, for a duel.

33
00:03:02,043 --> 00:03:06,696
Imam Malik(امام مالك) was asked about the ones, who stand out in front of the army and asked for a duel,

34
00:03:06,776 --> 00:03:07,156
he said:

35
00:03:07,204 --> 00:03:12,697
It depends on his intentions, if he's doing it for the sake of Allah, I do not see a problem with that,

36
00:03:13,333 --> 00:03:15,808
since that was the tradition of the ones before us.

37
00:03:16,176 --> 00:03:19,160
Imam As-Shafie(إمام ألشَّافعي) said: I don't see a problem with duels.

38
00:03:20,271 --> 00:03:28,333
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says: Know that duels during wars and accepting the invitation to it is the way of the heroes.

39
00:03:28,861 --> 00:03:37,878
It is a badge of honor for the brave men and it has been their pride, after Islam and before it.

40
00:03:39,592 --> 00:03:43,353
Amr Bin Abd Wud(عمروبن عبدود), one of the greatest fighters of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

41
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:46,812
During the Battle of Al-Khandaq(ألخندق), the trench came out asking for a duel.

42
00:03:47,199 --> 00:03:52,967
Amr Bin Abd Wud(عمروبن عبدود) was quite a formidable opponent.

43
00:03:54,269 --> 00:03:56,459
He was an old man at that time.

44
00:03:58,332 --> 00:04:04,030
I think it's a bit of an exaggeration but some say that he was over 80 years of age or something.

45
00:04:05,181 --> 00:04:10,933
But sometimes, you know, not all of these, details, tend to be authentic.

46
00:04:11,830 --> 00:04:18,251
Anyway, he was famous as being a very brave man and a very strong fighter.

47
00:04:18,791 --> 00:04:21,781
