Al-Haris(ألحارث) is the eldest son of Abdul Mutalib(عبدالمطلب).

189
00:15:07,963 --> 00:15:09,976
Hamza(حمزه) faced Ut'ba(عُتْبَة), and killed him.

190
00:15:10,604 --> 00:15:12,790
And I faced Shaibah(شيبة) and killed him.

191
00:15:13,346 --> 00:15:17,524
While Obaidah(عبيدة) and Al-Walid(ألوليد), both injured each other and fell down.

192
00:15:17,979 --> 00:15:20,894
Hamza(حمزه) and myself, walked up to Al-Walid(ألوليد) and killed him.

193
00:15:21,269 --> 00:15:25,346
We then carried Obaidah(عبيدة) away, Obaidah(عبيدة) ended up dying shortly after that.

194
00:15:29,155 --> 00:15:31,800
So this was the first Mubariza(مُبَارزَة) of Muslims

195
00:15:31,885 --> 00:15:34,222
and that's why Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) says, about the Ayah(آية),

196
00:15:34,699 --> 00:15:39,343
هٰذانِ خَصمانِ اختَصَموا في رَبِّهِم ۖ

197
00:15:39,673 --> 00:15:50,865
فَالَّذينَ كَفَروا قُطِّعَت لَهُم ثِيابٌ مِن نارٍ يُصَبُّ مِن فَوقِ رُءوسِهِمُ الحَميمُ۞

198
00:15:51,483 --> 00:15:56,729
The Ayah(آية) that says on the Day of Judgment, two men will come and dispute,

199
00:15:57,785 --> 00:16:00,470
the issue of who was following Allah,

200
00:16:00,819 --> 00:16:04,922
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said this Ayah(آية) is talking about me,

201
00:16:05,859 --> 00:16:08,245
when we fought on that Mubariza(مُبَارزَة),

202
00:16:08,285 --> 00:16:13,577
because this was the first fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) in terms of one on one,

203
00:16:13,657 --> 00:16:17,874
even though there were some skirmishes before, but in terms of an army facing an army.

204
00:16:18,207 --> 00:16:19,087
This was the first time.

205
00:16:23,911 --> 00:16:24,633
CHAPTER 10

206
00:16:26,188 --> 00:16:29,990
The severe punishment for the one, who turns his back during battle.

207
00:16:33,029 --> 00:16:33,736
Allah says:

208
00:16:33,959 --> 00:16:46,555
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا إِذا لَقيتُمُ الَّذينَ كَفَروا زَحفًا فَلا تُوَلّوهُمُ الأَدبارَ۞

209
00:16:47,150 --> 00:16:57,454
وَمَن يُوَلِّهِم يَومَئِذٍ دُبُرَهُ إِلّا مُتَحَرِّفًا لِقِتالٍ أَو مُتَحَيِّزًا

210
00:16:57,925 --> 00:17:05,622
أَو مُتَحَيِّزًا إِلىٰ فِئَةٍ فَقَد باءَ بِغَضَبٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ

211
00:17:06,027 --> 00:17:10,480
وَمَأواهُ جَهَنَّمُ ۖ وَبِئسَ المَصيرُ۞

212
00:17:12,340 --> 00:17:19,373
O you have believed, when you meet those who disbelieve advancing for battle, do not turn to them your back.

213
00:17:19,508 --> 00:17:23,595
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا إِذا لَقيتُمُ الَّذينَ كَفَروا زَحفًا فَلا تُوَلّوهُمُ الأَدبارَ۞

214
00:17:24,363 --> 00:17:33,834
وَمَن يُوَلِّهِم يَومَئِذٍ دُبُرَهُ إِلّا مُتَحَرِّفًا لِقِتالٍ أَو مُتَحَيِّزًا إِلىٰ فِئَةٍ فَقَد باءَ بِغَضَبٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَمَأواهُ جَهَنَّمُ ۖ وَبِئسَ المَصيرُ۞

215
00:17:34,436 --> 00:17:38,095
And whoever turns his back to them on Such a day,

216
00:17:38,588 --> 00:17:43,442
unless swerving as a strategy for war, or joining another company,

217
00:17:43,815 --> 00:17:51,054
has certainly returned with anger from Allah and his refuge is hell, and retched is the destination.

218
00:17:51,462 --> 00:17:54,919
And that's Al-Anfal(ألأنفال) Verse 15 and 16.

219
00:17:56,621 --> 00:18:02,196
Realize that turning ones back in battle, is a major sin according to the consensus of the scholars

220
00:18:02,914 --> 00:18:06,712
and the one, who does it deserve the Wrath of Allah and His severe punishment.

221
00:18:07,589 --> 00:18:10,638
Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) narrated the Messenger of Allah said:

222
00:18:11,463 --> 00:18:14,186
Stay away from the seven destroyers of your deeds,

223
00:18:15,178 --> 00:18:17,503
Associating another deity with Allah, Shirk(شرك),

224
00:18:17,836 --> 00:18:19,101
Sorcery, Sihr(سحر),

225
00:18:19,260 --> 00:18:20,125
Murder. Al-Qatl(ألقتل),

226
00:18:20,688 --> 00:18:22,448
asserping the wealth of an orphan,

227
00:18:22,958 --> 00:18:23,815
عكرمال اليتيم

228
00:18:24,395 --> 00:18:26,143
dealing with interest, Riba(رباء),

229
00:18:27,950 --> 00:18:30,648
turning one's back during battle,

230
00:18:30,950 --> 00:18:33,679
and accusing the chaste with adultery and fornication.

231
00:18:34,218 --> 00:18:35,626
And by the way with this last one,

232
00:18:39,292 --> 00:18:42,586
the Muslims knows the Hukm(حكم) of Zina(زنا),

233
00:18:42,673 --> 00:18:45,276
they know the outcome of drinking alcohol,

234
00:18:45,316 --> 00:18:46,617
they know the outcome of murder,

235
00:18:47,062 --> 00:18:54,442
but many times people don't know the Hukum(حكم) of accusing a chaste woman or man with Zina(زنا).

236
00:18:55,554 --> 00:19:00,109
And talking about these issues without having evidence.

237
00:19:00,547 --> 00:19:05,532
This is one of the areas, and this is a very dangerous crime because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ said:

238
00:19:05,865 --> 00:19:16,376
وَالَّذينَ يَرمونَ المُحصَناتِ ثُمَّ لَم يَأتوا بِأَربَعَةِ شُهَداءَ فَاجلِدوهُم ثَمانينَ جَلدَةً

239
00:19:17,063 --> 00:19:24,716
فَاجلِدوهُم ثَمانينَ جَلدَةً وَلا تَقبَلوا لَهُم شَهادَةً أَبَدًا ۚ

240
00:19:25,454 --> 00:19:29,430
وَأُولٰئِكَ هُمُ الفاسِقونَ۞

241
00:19:29,630 --> 00:19:34,567
That they should be lash 80 times, and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ said that their Shahadah(شَهَادَة) should never be accepted,

242
00:19:34,970 --> 00:19:36,025
and they are fasiq(فاسق).

243
00:19:37,582 --> 00:19:43,717
So it's very, very dangerous thing one should never ever accuse, and especially when it comes to women.

244
00:19:44,304 --> 00:19:49,558
One should never ever accused, a woman of such a crime without the evidence

245
00:19:49,598 --> 00:19:52,691
and the only evidence acceptable in Islam is four witnesses.

246
00:19:55,977 --> 00:19:57,508
And this Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(ألمسلم).

247
00:19:58,064 --> 00:20:03,166
If Jihad(جهاد) collective duty it becomes an individual duty, when the armies meet

248
00:20:04,522 --> 00:20:08,528
and turning one's back becomes prohibited the only exceptions are!

249
00:20:08,926 --> 00:20:14,085
We talked about the three conditions when Jihad(جهاد) becomes farz Aain(فرض عين), right!

250
00:20:14,863 --> 00:20:16,384
You remember them, what are they?

251
00:20:16,709 --> 00:20:23,226
Number one. When two armies meet, even if it was a Farz Kifaya(فرض كفاية) battle,

252
00:20:23,615 --> 00:20:25,656
but when the armies meet, it becomes Farz Aain(فرض عين).

253
00:20:26,174 --> 00:20:30,119
Second, Istafaar Al-Ameer(إستفارالأمير).

254
00:20:31,103 --> 00:20:34,615
And number three, when the enemy invades your land.

255
00:20:35,651 --> 00:20:37,122
The only exceptions are,

256
00:20:39,375 --> 00:20:43,287
the size of the enemy's army is more than twice that of the Muslims.

257
00:20:44,113 --> 00:20:46,880
Number two, swerving to take a new position.

258
00:20:47,690 --> 00:20:51,735
Number three, retreating to join another company of Muslims.

259
00:20:51,952 --> 00:20:58,034
Number four, being incapacitated, due to illness or having no access to a weapon.

260
00:20:59,778 --> 00:21:04,328
An-Nawwawi(ألنووِي) quotes Ar-Rafae(ألرفاعي)'s saying:

261
00:21:05,431 --> 00:21:09,400
If the enemy is more than double the size of the Muslims army,

262
00:21:09,821 --> 00:21:17,333
then if the Muslims think that if they would remain steadfast, they can win, then they should remain steadfast.

263
00:21:17,939 --> 00:21:22,567
But if they think that most likely they would perish, then it is allowed for them to retreat,

264
00:21:23,067 --> 00:21:27,012
but it's better for them to fight, even if they think they would be killed.

265
00:21:27,504 --> 00:21:31,028
Now this issue apparently there's difference of opinion on.

266
00:21:32,132 --> 00:21:34,206
Because An-Nawwawi(ألنووِي) comments and he says that

267
00:21:35,184 --> 00:21:38,279
retreat in this situation is not mandatory but it's recommended.

268
00:21:38,399 --> 00:21:40,973
So for An-Nawwawi(ألنووِي), it's recommended to retreat,

269
00:21:41,517 --> 00:21:43,092
if you think that you would perish.

270
00:21:44,830 --> 00:21:51,470
The Mazhab(مذهب) of Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ), is that if the enemy's army is twice the size of the Muslims

271
00:21:52,061 --> 00:21:57,228
and the Muslims think that most likely they would perish, if they fight,

272
00:21:57,426 --> 00:21:59,256
 and would be safe if they retreat,

273
00:21:59,788 --> 00:22:04,218
then it's better for them to retreat but it's also allowed for them to fight and seek martyrdom.

274
00:22:05,194 --> 00:22:06,595
So you see the difference of opinion.

275
00:22:09,186 --> 00:22:10,252
The view of Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس),

276
00:22:11,196 --> 00:22:17,201
the stronger opinion is that if a Muslim remains steadfast in a place that does not hurt the enemy,

277
00:22:17,791 --> 00:22:21,493
and only leads to his own demise, it is a sin to do so.

278
00:22:22,628 --> 00:22:26,072
An example would be a blind man fighting an enemy without any arms.

279
00:22:26,898 --> 00:22:33,572
But if the Muslims, stay and fight with courage, and with the intention of seeking martyrdom,

280
00:22:33,904 --> 00:22:37,967
and you can harm the enemy and he is killed, he would be rewarded by Allah.

281
00:22:38,070 --> 00:22:45,511
Now, keep in mind, brothers that in applying this Hukum(حكم) on today's circumstances,

282
00:22:45,869 --> 00:22:50,347
one needs to be very careful because the methods of battle today are very different.

283
00:22:51,766 --> 00:23:01,992
This new method of guerrilla warfare has greatly affected the rules of battle,

284
00:23:02,111 --> 00:23:07,913
so in guerrilla warfare really numbers is not that much of an issue anymore.

285
00:23:08,619 --> 00:23:14,662
So when applying these rules, maybe this issue needs to be studied further on modern forms of warfare,

286
00:23:15,035 --> 00:23:22,543
because in a guerrilla warfare if you have 300, 400 soldiers they can basically take on a huge army,

287
00:23:23,558 --> 00:23:29,932
because it is not an actually, an army facing one another on an open plain field,

288
00:23:30,298 --> 00:23:34,446
but it's Qarr Wal Farr(كرَّوالفر) method of attacking and retreating, attacking and retreating.

289
00:23:34,923 --> 00:23:38,057
So when we were talking about this Fiqh(فقه) of numbers here,

290
00:23:38,550 --> 00:23:46,015
I think, it cannot be applied straightforward as it is, in Fiqh(فقه) to the situations of today,

291
00:23:46,396 --> 00:23:48,340
and some other elements need to be looked at.

292
00:23:48,721 --> 00:23:55,964
Therefore, one needs to look at the Maqasid(مقاصد) of this Fiqh(فقه), rather than the, the numbers themselves.

293
00:23:56,419 --> 00:23:58,650
So, we can notice from the words of the scholars that,

294
00:23:59,197 --> 00:24:04,292
 it is only when you fear that you would be exterminated, then you should retreat.

295
00:24:06,411 --> 00:24:09,125
So that should be the guiding element.

296
00:24:09,650 --> 00:24:15,309
If an army feels that they would be exterminated then, they should not involve in a particular fight,

297
00:24:15,928 --> 00:24:20,842
whether the number is one to 10 or five to 10, or

298
00:24:22,406 --> 00:24:27,995
if they feel that they have a chance to make it and fight to survive, then they should not retreat.

299
00:24:29,066 --> 00:24:29,780
Allah says,

300
00:24:29,979 --> 00:24:37,706
يا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ حَرِّضِ المُؤمِنينَ عَلَى القِتالِ ۚ

301
00:24:38,190 --> 00:24:45,539
إِن يَكُن مِنكُم عِشرونَ صابِرونَ يَغلِبوا مِائَتَينِ ۚ

302
00:24:46,028 --> 00:24:55,865
وَإِن يَكُن مِنكُم مِائَةٌ يَغلِبوا أَلفًا مِنَ الَّذينَ كَفَروا

303
00:24:56,505 --> 00:25:03,287
مِنَ الَّذينَ كَفَروا بِأَنَّهُم قَومٌ لا يَفقَهونَ۞

304
00:25:03,741 --> 00:25:11,265
الآنَ خَفَّفَ اللَّهُ عَنكُم وَعَلِمَ أَنَّ فيكُم ضَعفًا ۚ

305
00:25:11,641 --> 00:25:20,299
فَإِن يَكُن مِنكُم مِائَةٌ صابِرَةٌ يَغلِبوا مِائَتَينِ ۚ

306
00:25:20,632 --> 00:25:29,078
وَإِن يَكُن مِنكُم أَلفٌ يَغلِبوا أَلفَينِ بِإِذنِ اللَّهِ ۗ

307
00:25:29,441 --> 00:25:33,561
وَاللَّهُ مَعَ الصّابِرينَ۞

308
00:25:33,916 --> 00:25:37,977
If there are among you 20 steadfast, they would overcome 200.

309
00:25:38,517 --> 00:25:42,989
And if they are among 100 steadfast, they would overcome 1000 of those who have disbelieved,

310
00:25:43,354 --> 00:25:45,775
because they are a people who do not understand.

311
00:25:46,790 --> 00:25:51,932
Now Allah has lightened the hardship for you, and He knows that among you is weakness.

312
00:25:52,385 --> 00:25:56,171
So if there are from you 100 steadfast, they will overcome 200.

313
00:25:56,655 --> 00:26:02,462
And if there are among you 1000, they will overcome 2000 by the permission of Allah.

314
00:26:02,770 --> 00:26:06,019
And Allah is with the steadfast, this is Al-Anfal(الأنفال) verse 65, 66.

315
00:26:06,452 --> 00:26:08,973
إِن يَكُن مِنكُم عِشرونَ صابِرونَ يَغلِبوا مِائَتَينِ ۚ

316
00:26:09,489 --> 00:26:14,401
وَإِن يَكُن مِنكُم مِائَةٌ يَغلِبوا أَلفًا مِنَ الَّذينَ كَفَروا بِأَنَّهُم قَومٌ لا يَفقَهونَ۞

317
00:26:14,679 --> 00:26:22,072
الآنَ خَفَّفَ اللَّهُ عَنكُم وَعَلِمَ أَنَّ فيكُم ضَعفًا ۚ فَإِن يَكُن مِنكُم مِائَةٌ صابِرَةٌ يَغلِبوا مِائَتَينِ ۚ

318
00:26:22,390 --> 00:26:27,553
وَإِن يَكُن مِنكُم أَلفٌ يَغلِبوا أَلفَينِ بِإِذنِ اللَّهِ ۗ وَاللَّهُ مَعَ الصّابِرينَ۞

319
00:26:29,378 --> 00:26:32,342
Ibn Mubarak(إبن المبارك) narrated that in Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) said,

320
00:26:32,445 --> 00:26:36,526
if one man retreats from three, he hasn't turned his back in battle.

321
00:26:36,897 --> 00:26:40,683
If he retreats from two than he has turned his back in battle.

322
00:26:40,723 --> 00:26:43,953
So that's the determinant factor in terms of numbers.

323
00:26:44,390 --> 00:26:46,247
Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) in his Tafseer(تفسير), he said:

324
00:26:48,147 --> 00:26:51,697
As long as the enemy is more than twice the number of Muslims,

325
00:26:53,249 --> 00:26:57,602
And you'll notice here, Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) quoting Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) a lot.

326
00:26:58,657 --> 00:27:02,172
And again I said that, when it comes to the fuqaha(فقهاء) you would find that

327
00:27:02,252 --> 00:27:06,302
the Fiqh(فقه) of Jihad(جهاد) among the scholars of Andalus(أندلس) is a bit more lively,

328
00:27:06,720 --> 00:27:08,642
because it was something that they lived.

329
00:27:08,762 --> 00:27:10,348
I mean that was the land of Jihad(جهاد) and Ribat(رباط),

330
00:27:11,030 --> 00:27:13,464
unlike, for example, when you look at the Tafseer(تفسير) of Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر),

331
00:27:13,498 --> 00:27:17,376
you don't find a lot of details like you would find with Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي).

332
00:27:17,456 --> 00:27:21,113
Because the experiences of a scholar do affect the way they look at things.

333
00:27:21,319 --> 00:27:24,230
Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) for example because he himself was involved in Jihad(جهاد),

334
00:27:24,669 --> 00:27:29,628
one of the most important references when it comes to Jihad(جهاد) is the volume of his Fatawa(فتاوى),

335
00:27:30,112 --> 00:27:32,240
an entire volume which was on Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

336
00:27:33,796 --> 00:27:37,162
As long as the enemy is more than twice the number of Muslims,

337
00:27:38,233 --> 00:27:41,889
by the way when I am mentioning the Mujallad(مجلد) of Jihad(جهاد), by Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه),

338
00:27:41,929 --> 00:27:45,643
I would say that the brothers who are interested in the Fiqh(فقه) of Jihad(جهاد) should go back to that reference.

339
00:27:45,841 --> 00:27:48,519
It is one of the excellent references on the Fiqh(فقه) of Jihad(جهاد).

340
00:27:49,234 --> 00:27:53,125
It should be part of your library if this, if the aspect of Fiqh(فقه) interests you.

341
00:27:54,236 --> 00:27:56,833
If you're looking at the Fazail(فضائل), there's nothing that beats Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس).

342
00:27:57,357 --> 00:27:59,238
Even though Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) does talk about Fiqh(فقه),

343
00:27:59,968 --> 00:28:04,389
but it's, not as elaborate and detailed as Fatawa Ibn Taymiyah(فتاوى اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه).

344
00:28:06,818 --> 00:28:10,254
As long as the enemy is more than twice the number of Muslims they can retreat,

345
00:28:10,746 --> 00:28:12,667
but being steadfast and fighting is better.

346
00:28:13,167 --> 00:28:15,873
The Battle of Mu'tah(مَؤتَة) and Muslims were only 3000,

347
00:28:16,595 --> 00:28:23,318
and they faced the Roman army of 200,000, Roman soldiers and 100,000 Arab soldiers.

348
00:28:23,873 --> 00:28:31,196
It was also, it is also mentioned that when Tariq(طارق) opened Andlusiya(أندلوسيه) he only had 1700 soldiers.

349
00:28:31,877 --> 00:28:33,330
Other references say 7000,

350
00:28:33,671 --> 00:28:35,679
while his enemy was 70,000 strong.

351
00:28:36,459 --> 00:28:42,025
Imam Malik(إمام مالك) was asked about the Muslim facing 10 enemy soldiers should you fight them, or retreat,

352
00:28:42,144 --> 00:28:44,248
he said: Both options are allowed for him.

353
00:28:45,835 --> 00:28:46,095
Tayeb(طيب),

354
00:28:46,619 --> 00:28:48,159
There's a hadith of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

355
00:28:48,246 --> 00:28:50,746
ولا يُغْلَبُ اثنا عشرَ ألفًا من قِلَّةٍ

356
00:28:52,389 --> 00:28:56,640
An army of 12,000 would never be defeated due to fewness,

357
00:28:56,800 --> 00:29:01,976
and this is Narrated by Abu Daud(أبوداؤد), Al Sunnan Al-Kubra(ألسنن ألكبرى), At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ), Ad-Darimi(ألدارمي), Al-Hakim(ألحَاكِم).

358
00:29:03,952 --> 00:29:05,711
So Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says:

359
00:29:05,751 --> 00:29:10,395
Most of the scholars consider this Hadith(حديث) to be an exception from the rule set by the verse

360
00:29:11,184 --> 00:29:14,605
that as long as the enemy is more than twice your number, you can retreat.

361
00:29:15,089 --> 00:29:19,569
The scholars say that this rule applies to armies less than 12,000 in numbers.

362
00:29:20,101 --> 00:29:27,294
However, if the Muslim army has 12,000 or more, they cannot turn their back no matter how large the enemy is.

363
00:29:28,776 --> 00:29:34,041
If the Muslims reach the number of 12,000, good trained fighters,

364
00:29:35,634 --> 00:29:38,760
then no matter what the size of the enemy army is, they should not retreat.

365
00:29:42,459 --> 00:29:43,031
Due to the Hadith(حديث).

366
00:29:43,111 --> 00:29:45,246
ولا يُغْلَبُ اثنا عشرَ ألفًا من قِلَّةٍ

367
00:29:45,729 --> 00:29:48,293
So the Hadith(حديث) says: They will not be defeated, due to fewness.

368
00:29:49,126 --> 00:29:51,803
If they're defeated it would be because of another reason,

369
00:29:52,057 --> 00:30:00,002
either disobedience of the Ameer(أمير), sins, disunity, but it's not due to lack of numbers,

370
00:30:00,407 --> 00:30:01,828
 even if they're facing a million.

371
00:30:02,455 --> 00:30:04,478
So the Hadith(حديث) does not guarantee that they would win,

372
00:30:05,121 --> 00:30:07,981
the Hadith(حديث) is guarantying that they will not lose due to numbers.

373
00:30:09,692 --> 00:30:10,700
Did you get the meaning of the Hadith(حديث).?

374
00:30:12,454 --> 00:30:15,275
The next few pages are not in your notes, unfortunately,

375
00:30:17,227 --> 00:30:22,309
these were few pages that somehow apparently I forgot to translate.

376
00:30:23,825 --> 00:30:26,777
It is a section on Allah is with the Mujahideen(مجاهدين).

377
00:30:29,347 --> 00:30:31,840
We can provide you with the notes later on In Sha Allah(إنْ شاءالله).

378
00:30:33,681 --> 00:30:37,808
Allah is with His creation in two forms,

379
00:30:37,896 --> 00:30:41,073
Number one, Maeyyah Aamah(معية عامة),

380
00:30:41,390 --> 00:30:46,485
Allah is with all of His creation, in terms of His knowledge and His Qudra(قدرة).

381
00:30:48,285 --> 00:30:52,936
The knowledge of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and the Qudra(قدرة) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ encompasses all of the Creation.

382
00:30:54,282 --> 00:30:55,368
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

383
00:30:55,820 --> 00:31:00,056
هُوَ الَّذي خَلَقَ السَّماواتِ وَالأَرضَ في سِتَّةِ أَيّامٍ ثُمَّ استَوىٰ عَلَى العَرشِ ۚ

384
00:31:00,757 --> 00:31:07,492
يَعلَمُ ما يَلِجُ فِي الأَرضِ وَما يَخرُجُ مِنها وَما يَنزِلُ مِنَ السَّماءِ وَما يَعرُجُ فيها ۖ وَهُوَ مَعَكُم أَينَ ما كُنتُم ۚ

385
00:31:07,991 --> 00:31:09,507
وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعمَلونَ بَصيرٌ۞

386
00:31:10,626 --> 00:31:13,520
He it is, Who created the heavens and the earth in six days,

387
00:31:14,346 --> 00:31:17,037
and is more ever firmly established on the throne.

388
00:31:17,728 --> 00:31:21,450
He knows what enters within the earth and what comes forth out of it.

389
00:31:22,228 --> 00:31:25,903
What comes down from the heaven and what mounts up to it,

390
00:31:26,268 --> 00:31:35,187
and He is with you, wherever you may be, and Allah sees well, all that you do.

391
00:31:35,267 --> 00:31:36,694
And this is Al-Hadid(ألحديد) verse Four.

392
00:31:38,171 --> 00:31:40,967
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says: In Surat Mujadla(سورة المجادلة) verse 7.

393
00:31:43,179 --> 00:31:46,047
أَلَم تَرَ أَنَّ اللَّهَ يَعلَمُ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الأَرضِ ۖ

394
00:31:46,341 --> 00:31:51,087
ما يَكونُ مِن نَجوىٰ ثَلاثَةٍ إِلّا هُوَ رابِعُهُم وَلا خَمسَةٍ إِلّا هُوَ سادِسُهُم

395
00:31:51,746 --> 00:31:55,636
وَلا أَدنىٰ مِن ذٰلِكَ وَلا أَكثَرَ إِلّا هُوَ مَعَهُم أَينَ ما كانوا ۖ

396
00:31:56,081 --> 00:31:59,977
ثُمَّ يُنَبِّئُهُم بِما عَمِلوا يَومَ القِيامَةِ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ بِكُلِّ شَيءٍ عَليمٌ۞

397
00:32:02,377 --> 00:32:07,070
See you not that Allah does know all that is in the heavens and on earth.

398
00:32:08,189 --> 00:32:12,862
There is not a secret consultation between the three, but Allah is their fourth,

399
00:32:13,880 --> 00:32:21,233
nor between five, but Allah is there six nor between fewer nor more but He is with them, wherever they may be.

400
00:32:21,820 --> 00:32:24,941
And in the end, will He tell them the truth of their conduct.

401
00:32:25,392 --> 00:32:28,636
On the day of judgment for Allah has full knowledge of all things.

402
00:32:29,515 --> 00:32:32,324
So this is general, presence of Allah.

403
00:32:32,904 --> 00:32:36,842
But then there's a special Presence of Allah and that says his presence with Al-Mujahideen(ألمجاهدين).

404
00:32:38,072 --> 00:32:41,279
This is a special presence with the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) and with the Saliheen(صالحين).

405
00:32:42,779 --> 00:32:45,674
For example, in the Jihad(جهاد) of Musa(موسى) with Firaun(فرعون).

406
00:32:47,698 --> 00:32:52,877
When Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ told Musa(موسى) and Harun(هارون), to go to the court of Firaun(فرعون).

407
00:32:53,591 --> 00:32:57,985
And you know, this is the one situation that,

408
00:33:00,032 --> 00:33:03,889
I don't really think that we will appreciate what Musa(موسى) and Harun(هارون) were going through

409
00:33:04,024 --> 00:33:06,240
because we have not lived those circumstances.

410
00:33:07,025 --> 00:33:11,120
Musa عليه السّلام left Egypt because he was wanted dead are alive.

411
00:33:12,120 --> 00:33:15,704
They wanted to execute him because he killed an Egyptian.

412
00:33:16,477 --> 00:33:20,466
He left Egypt for 10 years, left his family left his country.

413
00:33:21,744 --> 00:33:22,141
Right!

414
00:33:22,371 --> 00:33:23,260
And he's fugitive.

415
00:33:24,450 --> 00:33:27,272
And now Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is not telling him just to sneak into Egypt,

416
00:33:27,352 --> 00:33:31,940
Allah is telling you to go publicly and goes straight to Firaun(فرعون) and to tell Firaun(فرعون), I want you to follow me.

417
00:33:32,177 --> 00:33:34,694
 How can you pull that together.

418
00:33:36,712 --> 00:33:38,788
So for Musa(موسى) it was a different difficult command.

419
00:33:38,828 --> 00:33:41,157
And he said: He and Haroon(هارون) they said:

420
00:33:41,284 --> 00:33:44,079
قالا رَبَّنا إِنَّنا نَخافُ أَن يَفرُطَ عَلَينا أَو أَن يَطغىٰ۞

421
00:33:44,464 --> 00:33:46,845
O Allah, We are afraid that we might be killed.

422
00:33:48,655 --> 00:33:49,845
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ told them:

423
00:33:50,314 --> 00:33:53,676
قالَ لا تَخافا ۖ إِنَّني مَعَكُما أَسمَعُ وَأَرىٰ۞

424
00:33:54,366 --> 00:33:57,914
Don't be afraid, I am with you. I see, and I hear.

425
00:33:59,073 --> 00:34:00,413
Don't be worry, I'm with you.

426
00:34:01,524 --> 00:34:03,722
So this is a special presence of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

427
00:34:05,397 --> 00:34:06,444
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says,

428
00:34:06,841 --> 00:34:17,608
فَلا تَهِنوا وَتَدعوا إِلَى السَّلمِ وَأَنتُمُ الأَعلَونَ وَاللَّهُ مَعَكُم وَلَن يَتِرَكُم أَعمالَكُم۞

429
00:34:18,027 --> 00:34:26,400
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says: So be not weak and ask not for peace,

430
00:34:26,908 --> 00:34:29,805
while you are having the upper hand, Allah is with you.

431
00:34:30,019 --> 00:34:31,765
Why are you asking for peace, when Allah is with you.?

432
00:34:32,273 --> 00:34:35,388
Why are you giving in what Allah is with you, you don't really need anybody else.?

433
00:34:37,961 --> 00:34:41,682
And He will never decrease the reward of your good deeds.

434
00:34:43,071 --> 00:34:45,325
Or when Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) in the cave.

435
00:34:45,658 --> 00:34:48,575
إِذ يَقولُ لِصاحِبِهِ لا تَحزَن إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَنا ۖ

436
00:34:49,329 --> 00:34:54,635
He is telling to his companion: Don't be saddened, Allah is with us!

437
00:34:56,254 --> 00:35:03,729
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says whenever the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) faults on a certain aspect of his worship or commit sins,

438
00:35:04,499 --> 00:35:06,957
he becomes similar to the enemy in that aspect.

439
00:35:08,205 --> 00:35:10,695
And that would lead to darkness entering his heart.

440
00:35:11,436 --> 00:35:17,497
So, when you commit a sin, you become similar to the enemy, in that particular area,

441
00:35:17,616 --> 00:35:19,670
according to how many sins are committed.

442
00:35:20,281 --> 00:35:22,916
That is how similar, you become with the enemy.

443
00:35:25,265 --> 00:35:29,255
It could lead to him suffering from some fear and weakness,

444
00:35:29,727 --> 00:35:32,115
and thus would become more attached to this life

445
00:35:32,918 --> 00:35:38,037
and the effects of these sins of the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is proportionate to the magnitude of the sin.

446
00:35:39,354 --> 00:35:43,485
Don't you see what happened during the Battle of Hunain(حنين), when one of the Muslims said:

447
00:35:43,623 --> 00:35:46,769
We are not going to be defeated because of our numbers, one of the Muslims said:

448
00:35:47,380 --> 00:35:49,047
لن نغلب اليوم أن قلة

449
00:35:50,396 --> 00:35:53,874
Because the Muslims were 12,000, the Muslims never amassed such a huge army.

450
00:35:54,898 --> 00:35:58,232
10,000, who came to Fath-e-Makkah(فتح مكة), two Thousand from Muslim At-Fath(مسلم الفتح),

451
00:35:58,415 --> 00:36:01,603
the ones who became Muslim in Makkah, 12,000.

452
00:36:01,825 --> 00:36:04,087
So the Muslims, saw this and they were very impressed.

453
00:36:04,190 --> 00:36:07,673
He said: We cannot lose this battle, 12000 strong.

454
00:36:08,873 --> 00:36:18,334
That was a sin! Why was it a sin, because those are the criteria of the Kuffar(كفار).

455
00:36:19,119 --> 00:36:21,437
It is the Kuffar(كفار), who look at numbers, who look at equipment,

456
00:36:22,230 --> 00:36:24,449
but the Muslim looks at the assistance of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

457
00:36:25,731 --> 00:36:29,600
For the Muslims victory comes from Allah, it doesn't come from numbers or equipments.

458
00:36:30,612 --> 00:36:38,136
لَقَد نَصَرَكُمُ اللَّهُ في مَواطِنَ كَثيرَةٍ ۙ وَيَومَ حُنَينٍ ۙ

459
00:36:38,556 --> 00:36:46,713
وَيَومَ حُنَينٍ ۙ إِذ أَعجَبَتكُم كَثرَتُكُم فَلَم تُغنِ عَنكُم شَيئًا

460
00:36:47,047 --> 00:36:55,601
وَضاقَت عَلَيكُمُ الأَرضُ بِما رَحُبَت ثُمَّ وَلَّيتُم مُدبِرينَ۞

461
00:36:58,142 --> 00:37:00,994
وَيَومَ حُنَينٍ ۙ إِذ أَعجَبَتكُم كَثرَتُكُم

462
00:37:02,856 --> 00:37:06,105
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says: On the day of Hunain(حنين), you're impressed with your numbers,

463
00:37:06,399 --> 00:37:08,089
فَلَم تُغنِ عَنكُم شَيئًا

464
00:37:08,153 --> 00:37:11,088
They did you no good! They did you no good!

465
00:37:12,889 --> 00:37:13,881
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

466
00:37:15,699 --> 00:37:24,010
Don't you see what happened during the battle, assuredly Allah did help you in many battlefields.

467
00:37:24,534 --> 00:37:28,113
And on the day of Hunain(حنين) behold your great numbers, elated you,

468
00:37:28,875 --> 00:37:30,192
but they availed you not.

469
00:37:32,034 --> 00:37:33,161
And Allah said about in Uhud(أحَد).

470
00:37:33,700 --> 00:37:40,719
إِنَّ الَّذينَ تَوَلَّوا مِنكُم يَومَ التَقَى الجَمعانِ إِنَّمَا استَزَلَّهُمُ الشَّيطانُ بِبَعضِ ما كَسَبوا ۖ

471
00:37:41,139 --> 00:37:44,121
وَلَقَد عَفَا اللَّهُ عَنهُم ۗ إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفورٌ حَليمٌ۞

472
00:37:45,100 --> 00:37:52,396
Those of you, who turn back on the day the two hosts met, it was Satan who caused them to fail

473
00:37:52,936 --> 00:37:57,564
because of some evil they had done, but Allah has blotted out their fault.

474
00:37:58,040 --> 00:38:00,620
For Allah is oft forgiving, most Forbearing,

475
00:38:00,763 --> 00:38:02,247
and this is Al-Imran(ألعمران) Verse 155.

476
00:38:03,152 --> 00:38:07,254
In the Battle of Uhud(أحَد), the defeat on that day was, because of,

477
00:38:07,658 --> 00:38:08,412
what was the reason?

478
00:38:10,182 --> 00:38:11,905
Disobeying Rasool Allah ﷺ.

479
00:38:13,786 --> 00:38:20,600
There was a small hill, Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed 50 archers to take that post.

480
00:38:21,975 --> 00:38:24,281
And then you have maybe one kilometer distance

481
00:38:24,328 --> 00:38:27,233
and then you have the mountain Uhud(أحَد), which is about eight kilometers long.

482
00:38:29,035 --> 00:38:37,909
So, the Muslims had their front facing the enemy,

483
00:38:38,965 --> 00:38:42,568
but then their flank was to this small hill.

484
00:38:44,840 --> 00:38:50,245
And Rasool Allah ﷺ felt that the Muslims could be attacked from behind.

485
00:38:50,888 --> 00:38:53,396
So he appointed these 50 archers to protect them.

486
00:38:54,539 --> 00:38:56,249
Rasool Allah ﷺ told these archers.

487
00:38:58,082 --> 00:39:03,996
If you see us winning, Do not come down, if you see us losing, do not come down,

488
00:39:04,067 --> 00:39:07,120
even if you see vultures, eating our dead bodies.

489
00:39:08,543 --> 00:39:13,413
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying: I don't want you to help me, in the fighting, I just wanted to stay there and protect our backs.

490
00:39:13,563 --> 00:39:14,230
 That's it.!

491
00:39:15,595 --> 00:39:20,100
And brothers, this illustrates the importance of following the order,

492
00:39:22,124 --> 00:39:24,850
and when the order is specific don't make a judgment on your own.

493
00:39:26,377 --> 00:39:30,586
Rasool Allah ﷺ gave them a specific order, even if you see us dying don't come down,

494
00:39:30,619 --> 00:39:33,825
and if you see us winning do not come down, he made it very clear.

495
00:39:34,777 --> 00:39:35,506
The Muslims won.

496
00:39:36,775 --> 00:39:39,800
The enemies were on the run,

497
00:39:40,340 --> 00:39:44,073
and one of the Sahabah(صحابه) said: We could see the khalakhal(خلاخل) of their women.

498
00:39:44,637 --> 00:39:48,248
khalakhal(خلاخل) are the bracelets they have on their feet.

499
00:39:48,970 --> 00:39:49,948
We could see them running.

500
00:39:51,868 --> 00:39:57,053
Now, the Muslims, got involved in collecting the booty of war

501
00:39:57,148 --> 00:39:59,870
and these 50 men on top of the mountain, they thought it's all over.

502
00:40:00,561 --> 00:40:05,281
And they started getting a bit itchy

503
00:40:05,321 --> 00:40:10,546
and they were telling the Ameer(أمير), let us go and pick up some of these spoils of war.

504
00:40:11,154 --> 00:40:14,588
Abdullah Bin Jubair(عبدالله بن جبير) said: We have clear commands from Rasool Allah ﷺ to stay here.

505
00:40:17,501 --> 00:40:20,160
40 of them disobey the Ameer(أمير) and went down, 40.

506
00:40:21,096 --> 00:40:22,425
So only 10 remained on the mountain.

507
00:40:23,163 --> 00:40:31,305
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), this was his first experience in leading a cavalry in war.

508
00:40:33,131 --> 00:40:42,022
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), he detected with his eagle eyes that there's a weak point, there's a weak spot.

509
00:40:42,860 --> 00:40:45,731
So he made his move, alongside Iqrima Bin Abi Jahal(عكرمة بن أبي جهل),

510
00:40:46,144 --> 00:40:49,567
and they went around the mountain of Uhud(أحَد), according to one opinion, it's around the hill,

511
00:40:49,607 --> 00:40:52,315
but the other opinion which seems to be stronger if you see the battlefield,

512
00:40:52,727 --> 00:40:54,214
is that they went behind the mountain of Uhud(أحَد).

513
00:40:55,579 --> 00:40:58,594
And a fast horse can make that distance in a few minutes,

514
00:40:58,801 --> 00:41:01,224
it's about eight kilometers long but fast horses can make it.

515
00:41:01,626 --> 00:41:03,897
So they went all the way behind the mountain of Uhud(أحَد).

516
00:41:04,691 --> 00:41:07,356
And they attacked the Muslims from behind and they just cut through them.

517
00:41:08,889 --> 00:41:11,352
And that is when 70 of the Muslims were killed.

518
00:41:12,313 --> 00:41:17,278
It was a massacre among the Muslims, seventy of them got killed.

519
00:41:20,987 --> 00:41:24,350
Why did this all happen because of disobeying the commands Of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

520
00:41:26,588 --> 00:41:30,934
They made the judgment on their own, they said the battle is over.

521
00:41:34,394 --> 00:41:39,010
So, they lost in Hunain(حنين) because of sin, they lost in Uhud(أحَد) because of sin.

522
00:41:41,947 --> 00:41:42,740
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

523
00:41:42,780 --> 00:41:48,126
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا قاتِلُوا الَّذينَ يَلونَكُم مِنَ الكُفّارِ وَليَجِدوا فيكُم غِلظَةً ۚ

524
00:41:48,530 --> 00:41:50,382
وَاعلَموا أَنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ المُتَّقينَ۞

525
00:41:50,903 --> 00:41:56,973
