In the Name of Allah, on the Day of Judgment they are heavier on the scale than the mountain of Uhud(أحَد).

713
00:54:18,551 --> 00:54:24,745
Now brothers! This frail body and weak body of Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود),

714
00:54:26,197 --> 00:54:31,218
that weak hand, or thin hand was the hand that cut off the head of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل),

715
00:54:31,742 --> 00:54:32,869
the Firaun(فرعون) of this Ummah(امة).

716
00:54:34,036 --> 00:54:38,017
It wasn't a big, muscular wrestler who killed the Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل).

717
00:54:38,456 --> 00:54:39,496
It was Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود).

718
00:54:40,758 --> 00:54:45,893
He is the one, after a Muawiz(معوذ) and Ma'az Bin Afrah(معاذ بن أفراح), who fought with Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل)

719
00:54:45,933 --> 00:54:50,726
and the Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) was laying down and he wasn't dead yet, he was in his last moments.

720
00:54:52,051 --> 00:54:56,135
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود), he climbed over the chest of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل), when he was lying on his back,

721
00:54:56,341 --> 00:55:01,135
he climbed over him, and he held the sword, and he wanted to cut off the head of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل).

722
00:55:02,238 --> 00:55:04,725
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) not only was he short and slim,

723
00:55:05,170 --> 00:55:09,519
but he was also seen as being from a humble family in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

724
00:55:10,098 --> 00:55:12,311
He was a shepherd of goats.

725
00:55:12,883 --> 00:55:13,676
So Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) told him,

726
00:55:13,716 --> 00:55:16,662
لَقَدْ ارْتَقَيْتَ مُرْتَقًى صَعْبًا يَا رُوَيْعِي الْغَنَمِ

727
00:55:17,121 --> 00:55:19,980
You're climbing a very high peak you shepherd of goats.

728
00:55:20,724 --> 00:55:25,408
When he climbed on his chest, he said: You're climbing a very high peak, you shepherd of goats.

729
00:55:25,488 --> 00:55:28,360
I mean it's not even appropriate for you to be sitting on my chest,

730
00:55:29,424 --> 00:55:31,304
and that's when Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) cut off his head.

731
00:55:32,852 --> 00:55:37,017
So it's not really the body, it is not the physical strength, it is the heart.

732
00:55:37,645 --> 00:55:42,269
That's what you want to plant in the youth, Amal Qalb(أعمال ألقلب), strong hearts.

733
00:55:43,142 --> 00:55:45,925
The early Mujahideen(مجاهدين) were very cautious from committing sins

734
00:55:45,981 --> 00:55:49,368
because they knew the effect that had on their Jihad(جهاد).

735
00:55:50,282 --> 00:55:53,247
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) mentions in his history book,

736
00:55:53,978 --> 00:55:57,406
that one of the Muslims during the era of Sultan Az-Zahar Bin Bars(سلطان الزهر بن برص)

737
00:55:58,232 --> 00:56:01,386
used to make Jihad(جهاد) on his horse, which was a strong and fast horse,

738
00:56:02,076 --> 00:56:05,901
but one day his horse was acting very different, it was slow and disobedient,

739
00:56:06,590 --> 00:56:08,700
so he was astonished by the reaction of his horse,

740
00:56:09,157 --> 00:56:15,497
but then he realized the reason why, and remembered that he has fed his horse food purchased with a counterfeit coin.

741
00:56:17,283 --> 00:56:23,260
So he could feel the resistance of the horse because of the Haram(حرام) food, that he gave it.

742
00:56:24,020 --> 00:56:26,596
O Mujahid(مُجَاهِد), beware of disobeying Allah,

743
00:56:27,078 --> 00:56:29,882
sins would weaken your heart and defeat your will,

744
00:56:30,674 --> 00:56:36,667
purify your heart from contaminations and spark in, its darkness, the light of Tawakkul(توكل) and Yaqeen(يقين)

745
00:56:37,294 --> 00:56:44,464
and have courage of the One, Who is certain, that death is inevitable and that nothing can protect you from it.

746
00:56:44,988 --> 00:56:53,605
أَينَما تَكونوا يُدرِككُمُ المَوتُ وَلَو كُنتُم في بُروجٍ مُشَيَّدَةٍ ۗ

747
00:56:54,263 --> 00:57:03,108
وَإِن تُصِبهُم حَسَنَةٌ يَقولوا هٰذِهِ مِن عِندِ اللَّهِ ۖ

748
00:57:03,528 --> 00:57:10,973
وَإِن تُصِبهُم سَيِّئَةٌ يَقولوا هٰذِهِ مِن عِندِكَ ۚ

749
00:57:11,328 --> 00:57:16,529
قُل كُلٌّ مِن عِندِ اللَّهِ ۖ

750
00:57:16,910 --> 00:57:25,689
فَمالِ هٰؤُلاءِ القَومِ لا يَكادونَ يَفقَهونَ حَديثًا۞

751
00:57:26,576 --> 00:57:30,623
أَينَما تَكونوا يُدرِككُمُ المَوتُ وَلَو كُنتُم في بُروجٍ مُشَيَّدَةٍ ۗ

752
00:57:31,322 --> 00:57:34,356
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says: Wherever you are, that will find you out.

753
00:57:34,959 --> 00:57:38,177
Even if you are in towers, built up strong and high.

754
00:57:38,808 --> 00:57:40,483
There's no way to get away from death.

755
00:57:42,054 --> 00:57:45,118
And if Allah has destined for someone to be killed.

756
00:57:45,491 --> 00:57:47,126
Nothing can change that faith.

757
00:57:47,372 --> 00:57:48,118
 Allah says,

758
00:57:48,332 --> 00:57:59,781
ثُمَّ أَنزَلَ عَلَيكُم مِن بَعدِ الغَمِّ أَمَنَةً نُعاسًا يَغشىٰ طائِفَةً مِنكُم ۖ

759
00:58:00,295 --> 00:58:11,601
وَطائِفَةٌ قَد أَهَمَّتهُم أَنفُسُهُم يَظُنّونَ بِاللَّهِ غَيرَ الحَقِّ ظَنَّ الجاهِلِيَّةِ ۖ

760
00:58:12,070 --> 00:58:17,052
يَقولونَ هَل لَنا مِنَ الأَمرِ مِن شَيءٍ ۗ

761
00:58:17,420 --> 00:58:21,414
قُل إِنَّ الأَمرَ كُلَّهُ لِلَّهِ ۗ

762
00:58:21,610 --> 00:58:27,012
يُخفونَ في أَنفُسِهِم ما لا يُبدونَ لَكَ ۖ

763
00:58:27,416 --> 00:58:34,496
يَقولونَ لَو كانَ لَنا مِنَ الأَمرِ شَيءٌ ما قُتِلنا هاهُنا ۗ

764
00:58:34,965 --> 00:58:43,896
قُل لَو كُنتُم في بُيوتِكُم لَبَرَزَ الَّذينَ كُتِبَ عَلَيهِمُ القَتلُ إِلىٰ مَضاجِعِهِم ۖ

765
00:58:44,343 --> 00:58:51,643
وَلِيَبتَلِيَ اللَّهُ ما في صُدورِكُم وَلِيُمَحِّصَ ما في قُلوبِكُم ۗ

766
00:58:51,921 --> 00:58:56,188
وَاللَّهُ عَليمٌ بِذاتِ الصُّدورِ۞

767
00:58:56,715 --> 00:59:00,259
يَقولونَ لَو كانَ لَنا مِنَ الأَمرِ شَيءٌ ما قُتِلنا هاهُنا ۗ

768
00:59:00,632 --> 00:59:04,979
قُل لَو كُنتُم في بُيوتِكُم لَبَرَزَ الَّذينَ كُتِبَ عَلَيهِمُ القَتلُ إِلىٰ مَضاجِعِهِم ۖ

769
00:59:06,521 --> 00:59:11,132
They say to themselves, if we had anything, if we had had anything to do with this affair,

770
00:59:11,823 --> 00:59:14,211
we should not have been in this laughter here,

771
00:59:14,751 --> 00:59:20,412
say, even if you had remained in your homes, those for whom death was decreed,

772
00:59:20,818 --> 00:59:23,512
would certainly have gone forth to the place of their death.

773
00:59:24,778 --> 00:59:26,713
That's Al-Imran(ألعمران) Verse 154.

774
00:59:28,760 --> 00:59:31,689
There's a story of a man who fell down.

775
00:59:32,506 --> 00:59:35,828
Apparently, it's told that story happened in Saudia(سعودية).

776
00:59:35,868 --> 00:59:41,597
A man fell down from the seventh floor or something very high, landed on the pavement and he didn't die.

777
00:59:44,841 --> 00:59:48,695
All of the reasons for dying were there and he didn't die.

778
00:59:49,521 --> 00:59:56,002
So he was very amazed that he was actually alive so he stands up and he's so happy

779
00:59:56,470 --> 01:00:00,001
and people gather around him, and he is just celebrating that Allah has given him a new life.

780
01:00:00,970 --> 01:00:05,331
And he's telling to the people I'm gonna buy you some Pepsi(بيبسي), you know in Arabic you don't have a P.

781
01:00:06,227 --> 01:00:07,590
I'm gonna get you some Bebsi(بيبسي).

782
01:00:08,132 --> 01:00:11,672
So he crosses the street to go and buy them some Bebsi(بيبسي) and car rolls over him and he died.

783
01:00:14,585 --> 01:00:19,068
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has made an appointment with him, with the angel of death in the middle of the road,

784
01:00:19,179 --> 01:00:20,316
it wasn't on the pavement.

785
01:00:20,798 --> 01:00:24,307
And Allah brought him down from the building, down to the pavement

786
01:00:24,744 --> 01:00:29,779
and come to the exact place where he was destined to meet the angel of death.

787
01:00:30,284 --> 01:00:31,077
That's where he died.

788
01:00:33,260 --> 01:00:35,862
You cannot get away from it.

789
01:00:36,142 --> 01:00:40,099
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was looking for death, looking for it.

790
01:00:41,377 --> 01:00:45,112
You know, and you can see it in his letters to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and in his statements.

791
01:00:46,176 --> 01:00:48,644
In one of his letters to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), he said:

792
01:00:49,303 --> 01:00:53,907
And I have thrown myself in situations where I lost hope in living.

793
01:00:55,771 --> 01:00:58,049
ولقد اكتحمت حتى أن يست من الحياة

794
01:00:59,073 --> 01:01:00,899
Because in one of these battles.

795
01:01:01,492 --> 01:01:03,913
He got married after the battle was over, he got married,

796
01:01:03,993 --> 01:01:08,401
after the Battle of Yamamah(يمامة), he got married to the daughter Muja'ah(مجاعة)

797
01:01:10,051 --> 01:01:13,819
one of the leaders from Banu Hanifa(بنوحنيفة), he got married to his daughter.

798
01:01:14,781 --> 01:01:19,414
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was very upset that he got married and he sends him a very harsh letter he says:

799
01:01:19,713 --> 01:01:21,562
You're getting married and you're enjoying a women,

800
01:01:21,943 --> 01:01:26,299
when you have in your court, the bodies of 700 Muslims,

801
01:01:26,798 --> 01:01:30,576
I forgot the number who and their blood has not even dried yet.

802
01:01:32,012 --> 01:01:32,959
How could you do that?

803
01:01:33,166 --> 01:01:36,129
Because many Muslims died in the battle of Yamamah(يمامة).

804
01:01:37,070 --> 01:01:38,873
So Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) sends a letter back he's saying:

805
01:01:39,325 --> 01:01:41,857
I only got married after victory was complete.

806
01:01:43,436 --> 01:01:45,244
And then he's telling Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق)

807
01:01:45,896 --> 01:01:51,321
and I have thrown myself in situations in battle, where I have lost hope of living.

808
01:01:52,519 --> 01:01:53,376
And then he told him:

809
01:01:53,416 --> 01:01:59,757
And if my sadness, would revive the dead, they would have been revived.

810
01:02:01,241 --> 01:02:03,916
But this is the Qadar(قَدَر) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and nothing would change it.

811
01:02:04,511 --> 01:02:07,781
In other words, it was the Qadar(قَدَر) of Allah that these die men die,

812
01:02:08,177 --> 01:02:11,567
and if my love for them would make them live they would have lived.

813
01:02:12,969 --> 01:02:14,057
Because they are so dear to me.

814
01:02:16,350 --> 01:02:18,080
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) when he is dying, he said,

815
01:02:19,064 --> 01:02:25,879
there's not a single part of my body that was not struck by a sword, a spear, or an arrow,

816
01:02:26,217 --> 01:02:28,191
and here I am dying on my bed.

817
01:02:29,598 --> 01:02:31,951
So may the eyes of the cowards never get any sleep.

818
01:02:33,919 --> 01:02:38,037
He is saying that I've thrown myself in all these situations one after another.

819
01:02:38,586 --> 01:02:42,334
I have injuries all of all over my body and here I am dying on my bed.

820
01:02:46,064 --> 01:02:47,576
لا يغني حاضرون عن قدر

821
01:02:48,187 --> 01:02:51,605
Being cautious will not choose the Qadar(قَدَر) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

822
01:02:52,861 --> 01:02:56,120
O you who runs away from the battlefield,

823
01:02:56,635 --> 01:03:02,040
Realize that running away will not extend your life and being steadfast wouldn't shorten it.

824
01:03:03,374 --> 01:03:09,962
And remember that you have committed the grave sin, and you have clothed yourself with a cloak of humiliation.

825
01:03:11,097 --> 01:03:15,708
Aren't you worried that you might be taken as a prisoner and tortured until you give up your religion,

826
01:03:16,160 --> 01:03:18,255
so you end up losing this world and the last.

827
01:03:19,017 --> 01:03:22,945
Aren't you afraid that you might be taken, and then eventually killed.

828
01:03:23,961 --> 01:03:25,483
Whoever has any intelligence

829
01:03:25,993 --> 01:03:31,434
would realize that facing death when it's time, has approached is better than turning your back towards it.

830
01:03:32,085 --> 01:03:38,483
If your time of death is now, it's better for you to face it with your chest than to face it with your back.

831
01:03:40,171 --> 01:03:41,195
Rasool Allah ﷺ says,

832
01:03:41,989 --> 01:03:43,116
أقبلنًا غير مدبر

833
01:03:44,171 --> 01:03:46,681
Facing Shahadah(شَهَادَة) not running away from it.

834
01:03:49,882 --> 01:03:51,144
O you who runs away!

835
01:03:51,231 --> 01:03:56,225
Aren't you concerned that while you are running away a stray arrow might strike you and kill you.

836
01:03:56,519 --> 01:03:58,024
So you would end up being in hellfire.

837
01:03:59,773 --> 01:04:05,614
The stories of those who lost their religion because they did not fight, and were taken as prisoners are many.

838
01:04:06,646 --> 01:04:11,272
Al-Bayhaqi(ألبيهقي) narrates from Abdu Bin Abdur Rahim(عبدو بن عبدالرحيم).

839
01:04:11,670 --> 01:04:12,721
This is an interesting story,

840
01:04:13,475 --> 01:04:18,509
Abdu Bin Abdur Rahim(عبدو بن عبدالرحيم) narrates that we were in an army in the land of the Romans.

841
01:04:20,602 --> 01:04:22,166
And we had with us, a young man.

842
01:04:23,182 --> 01:04:27,782
Abdu Bin Abdur Rahim(عبدو بن عبدالرحيم) says: There was none among us who used to recite Qur'an better than him.

843
01:04:28,793 --> 01:04:34,472
 And he was the most knowledgeable among us, and he would spend his day fasting and his night praying.

844
01:04:36,164 --> 01:04:40,444
He said: While we were passing next to one of the Roman fortresses,

845
01:04:41,054 --> 01:04:45,538
 he saw this Christian woman and he fell in love with her.

846
01:04:45,633 --> 01:04:46,165
That's it!

847
01:04:46,371 --> 01:04:47,343
From one side,

848
01:04:48,621 --> 01:04:55,742
he was hooked to this woman, so he went to the fortress and he started speaking to her.

849
01:04:57,861 --> 01:05:00,984
He said: How can I get access to you?

850
01:05:01,127 --> 01:05:05,344
She said: Simple become Christian, and will open for you the gates.

851
01:05:06,237 --> 01:05:08,101
He became Christian and they open the gates for him.

852
01:05:08,944 --> 01:05:10,327
Abdu Bin Abdur Rahim(عبدو بن عبدالرحيم) said:

853
01:05:10,438 --> 01:05:16,922
When we left, we were extremely disheartened and saddened by what happened.

854
01:05:18,351 --> 01:05:24,526
He said: Then a long time passed, and we came back and we passed next to the same fortress.

855
01:05:25,148 --> 01:05:30,436
And we saw this young man standing up on one of the observation posts,

856
01:05:31,187 --> 01:05:33,851
along with Roman soldiers guarding the fortress.

857
01:05:35,202 --> 01:05:36,432
So he went to him and said,

858
01:05:37,091 --> 01:05:42,492
يا فلان ما فعل قرآن، ما فعلت بصلاتك وصيامك

859
01:05:42,809 --> 01:05:48,024
Oh, so and so! What happened to your Qur'an, what's happened to your good deeds, what's happened to your fasting?

860
01:05:48,270 --> 01:05:49,333
What's happened to your prayer.?

861
01:05:50,339 --> 01:05:55,272
He said: In the name of Allah, I remember nothing from Qur'an except one verse.

862
01:05:56,422 --> 01:05:58,814
And He recited to them the verse that he remembers.

863
01:05:59,541 --> 01:06:00,116
He says:

864
01:06:00,497 --> 01:06:03,560
رُبَما يَوَدُّ الَّذينَ كَفَروا لَو كانوا مُسلِمينَ۞

865
01:06:04,171 --> 01:06:08,786
ذَرهُم يَأكُلوا وَيَتَمَتَّعوا وَيُلهِهِمُ الأَمَلُ ۖ فَسَوفَ يَعلَمونَ۞

866
01:06:10,602 --> 01:06:13,798
He said: I remember nothing from Qur'an but one verse,

867
01:06:14,419 --> 01:06:15,774
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

868
01:06:15,854 --> 01:06:21,906
Again and again, will those who disbelieve, wish that they had bowed in Islam.

869
01:06:23,049 --> 01:06:26,230
Leave them alone to enjoy the good things of this life,

870
01:06:26,817 --> 01:06:31,154
and to please themselves, let false hope amuse them,

871
01:06:31,607 --> 01:06:34,369
soon will knowledge undeceive them,

872
01:06:35,075 --> 01:06:36,867
look at the particular Ayah(آية) that he remembered.

873
01:06:37,702 --> 01:06:40,505
رُبَما يَوَدُّ الَّذينَ كَفَروا لَو كانوا مُسلِمينَ۞

874
01:06:40,990 --> 01:06:44,785
Maybe one day the disbelievers would desire that they would be believers.

875
01:06:46,221 --> 01:06:54,177
Let them enjoy this life, the pleasures of this life and the false hope, because they will come to know the truth.

876
01:06:55,455 --> 01:06:59,902
I give this story, so that you can only ask the Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to give you Thabat(ثبات).

877
01:07:01,227 --> 01:07:06,986
However, when a Muslim fights sincerely, but then falls into captivity,

878
01:07:07,130 --> 01:07:11,976
and his enemy tried to mislead him, Allah would protect him and be on his side.

879
01:07:12,114 --> 01:07:16,471
An example would be the story of Abdullah Bin Hudhafa(عبدالله بن حذافة), the companion of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

880
01:07:16,511 --> 01:07:18,313
Did we talked about his story.

881
01:07:18,940 --> 01:07:21,987
Abdullah Bin Hudhafa(عبدالله بن حذافة) was captured by the Romans.

882
01:07:23,186 --> 01:07:26,921
The Romans were quite happy to have one of the Sahabah(صحابه),

883
01:07:27,365 --> 01:07:29,513
you know for them was the Sahabah(صحابه) was a legendary figure.

884
01:07:30,413 --> 01:07:35,419
Sahabah(صحابه), they would hear about them, all these strange legends, Sahabah(صحابه)!

885
01:07:36,028 --> 01:07:38,632
So the Roman king, he wanted to meet this man,

886
01:07:38,989 --> 01:07:40,683
so they brought him Abdullah Bin Hudhafa(عبدالله بن حذافة).

887
01:07:41,151 --> 01:07:42,711
He told him I want you to become Christian.

888
01:07:43,755 --> 01:07:45,027
Abdullah Bin Hudhafa(عبدالله بن حذافة) refused.

889
01:07:45,826 --> 01:07:50,007
He said: If you don't, this is what will happen to you.

890
01:07:51,299 --> 01:07:56,568
They had this huge pot with boiling water.

891
01:07:58,687 --> 01:08:01,870
So they brought one of the Muslim prisoners of war and they threw him in the water.

892
01:08:03,172 --> 01:08:04,252
Abdullah Bin Hudhafa(عبدالله بن حذافة) said:

893
01:08:05,188 --> 01:08:09,911
As soon as he landed in that water his flesh started just falling off the bones.

894
01:08:10,672 --> 01:08:14,115
It's so hot, it just separates the flesh from the bones.

895
01:08:16,510 --> 01:08:21,687
They said: If you don't become Christian, this is what we'll do.?

896
01:08:23,441 --> 01:08:24,028
He said: I won't!

897
01:08:25,695 --> 01:08:29,457
So they picked him up in order to throw him in the container.

898
01:08:30,394 --> 01:08:32,061
Abdullah Bin Hudhafa(عبدالله بن حذافة) started to cry.

899
01:08:33,592 --> 01:08:37,343
So the king said: We got him, he has softened.

900
01:08:37,925 --> 01:08:40,933
Now he is going to become Christian.

901
01:08:41,788 --> 01:08:47,140
Abdullah Bin Hudhafa(عبدالله بن حذافة) said: Don't think that the reason, why I cried, is because I feared death.

902
01:08:48,125 --> 01:08:54,704
The reason why I cried, is because I realized that I only have one soul.

903
01:08:55,614 --> 01:09:01,712
And I would have desire that Allah would give me souls, the number of hair that I have in my head,

904
01:09:02,577 --> 01:09:06,415
so that I could give them one after another, in the path of Allah.

905
01:09:10,073 --> 01:09:13,786
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), you see somebody boil in front of you and you see his flesh separating from the bone

906
01:09:13,841 --> 01:09:16,613
and then you wish that that happens to you, not once but 100 times,

907
01:09:18,518 --> 01:09:19,359
a 100 times!!!

908
01:09:19,907 --> 01:09:23,549
It's that I wish that I had as many souls as hair on my head,

909
01:09:24,113 --> 01:09:26,176
to give them in Sabeel-Lillah(سَبيل الله) one after another.

910
01:09:26,800 --> 01:09:28,253
The king was very impressed by that.

911
01:09:28,587 --> 01:09:29,335
He said: Listen!

912
01:09:30,404 --> 01:09:34,816
If you become Christian, I will marry you to my daughter and give you half of my kingdom,

913
01:09:35,753 --> 01:09:36,760
half of my kingdom!!!

914
01:09:37,229 --> 01:09:38,610
Abdullah Bin Hudhafa(عبدالله بن حذافة) said: No way!

915
01:09:39,157 --> 01:09:45,011
Now the king wanted to get just anything from Abdullah Bin Hudhafa(عبدالله بن حذافة).

916
01:09:45,051 --> 01:09:46,773
 He is trying everything and he's not getting anywhere.

917
01:09:47,408 --> 01:09:50,701
He says: Alright! If you kiss my forehead, I'm gonna release you.

918
01:09:51,622 --> 01:09:52,535
Just kiss my forehead!!!

919
01:09:53,717 --> 01:09:55,449
Abdullah Bin Hudhafa(عبدالله بن حذافة) thought about that and he said:

920
01:09:56,148 --> 01:10:02,799
Only if you're gonna release all of the Muslim prisoners of war with me.

921
01:10:04,124 --> 01:10:05,227
The King said: I agree!

922
01:10:05,918 --> 01:10:11,184
Abdullah Bin Hudhafa(عبدالله بن حذافة), he kisses him, and the king releases, all of the Muslim prisoners of war, all of them.

923
01:10:14,049 --> 01:10:16,183
Abdullah Bin Hudhafa(عبدالله بن حذافة) gets to Al-Madina,

924
01:10:16,299 --> 01:10:17,838
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) hears the news.

925
01:10:17,878 --> 01:10:20,071
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) stands up on the Mimber(ممبر) and says,

926
01:10:20,711 --> 01:10:22,030
حقٌ على كل مسلم

927
01:10:22,133 --> 01:10:26,031
It's a duty on every Muslim in Madina to go and kiss the forehead of Abdullah Bin Hudhafa(عبدالله بن حذافة).

928
01:10:27,752 --> 01:10:29,133
So Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ gave him Sabat(ثبات).

929
01:10:31,371 --> 01:10:33,939
This was narrated by Ibn Al- Athir(اِبْنِ ألأثِيْر).

930
01:10:35,043 --> 01:10:39,918
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says: It is not allowed for a Muslim to flee death.

931
01:10:41,125 --> 01:10:45,891
If there was no virtue and martyrdom, other than being spared the agony of death,

932
01:10:45,988 --> 01:10:50,978
that would have been sufficient enough to make a person refuse to retreat from the battlefield,

933
01:10:51,789 --> 01:10:52,493
Saqrat-Ul-Moat(سكرات الموت).

934
01:10:53,874 --> 01:10:57,210
Ali رضي الله عنه would encourage the Muslims to fight by saying:

935
01:10:57,567 --> 01:10:59,488
If you are not killed, you would die.

936
01:10:59,821 --> 01:11:05,666
In the Name of Allah 1000 strikes of a sword are less painful than dying on your bed.

937
01:11:06,475 --> 01:11:08,033
Saqrat-Ul-Moat(سكرات الموت) are very painful.

938
01:11:09,184 --> 01:11:10,763
The agony of death is very painful,

939
01:11:11,740 --> 01:11:19,791
and Ali(علي) is saying that 1000 strikes of a sword are gonna hurt you less than dying on your bed.

940
01:11:20,841 --> 01:11:25,069
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) is saying this is sufficient enough to make you wanted as Shaheed(شَهِيد).

941
01:11:25,657 --> 01:11:28,992
But then he says, in addition to that,

942
01:11:30,842 --> 01:11:36,093
the one who dies on his bed will suffer from the agony of death and after that the darkness and the horror of the grave,

943
01:11:36,459 --> 01:11:40,058
the questioning of the angels, the resurrection, the reckoning the weighing of deeds,

944
01:11:40,276 --> 01:11:41,792
and the crossing of the bridge,

945
01:11:43,300 --> 01:11:48,079
Shadad Bin Aus(شداد بن الأوس) would say death is the worst experience of this world, or the afterlife.

946
01:11:48,481 --> 01:11:53,270
It is worse than being cut by saws or scissors or boiling water.

947
01:11:53,973 --> 01:11:56,622
So which is better for you, dying in the path of Allah

948
01:11:56,697 --> 01:11:59,659
or dying on your bed, you decide for yourself,

949
01:12:02,070 --> 01:12:03,047
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

950
01:12:03,404 --> 01:12:14,607
يا أَيُّهَا النّاسُ اتَّقوا رَبَّكُم ۚ إِنَّ زَلزَلَةَ السّاعَةِ شَيءٌ عَظيمٌ۞

951
01:12:15,443 --> 01:12:28,165
يَومَ تَرَونَها تَذهَلُ كُلُّ مُرضِعَةٍ عَمّا أَرضَعَت وَتَضَعُ كُلُّ ذاتِ حَملٍ حَملَها

952
01:12:29,093 --> 01:12:39,091
وَتَضَعُ كُلُّ ذاتِ حَملٍ حَملَها وَتَرَى النّاسَ سُكارىٰ وَما هُم بِسُكارىٰ

953
01:12:39,694 --> 01:12:47,440
وَما هُم بِسُكارىٰ وَلٰكِنَّ عَذابَ اللَّهِ شَديدٌ۞

954
01:12:47,919 --> 01:12:52,030
يا أَيُّهَا النّاسُ اتَّقوا رَبَّكُم ۚ إِنَّ زَلزَلَةَ السّاعَةِ شَيءٌ عَظيمٌ۞

955
01:12:52,356 --> 01:12:53,839
O mankind Fear your Lord!

956
01:12:54,434 --> 01:12:58,765
For the convulsion of the Hour of judgment will be a terrible thing.

957
01:12:59,466 --> 01:13:04,063
يَومَ تَرَونَها تَذهَلُ كُلُّ مُرضِعَةٍ عَمّا أَرضَعَت وَتَضَعُ كُلُّ ذاتِ حَملٍ حَملَها

958
01:13:04,485 --> 01:13:08,363
وَتَرَى النّاسَ سُكارىٰ وَما هُم بِسُكارىٰ وَلٰكِنَّ عَذابَ اللَّهِ شَديدٌ۞

959
01:13:09,731 --> 01:13:10,798
The day you shall see it.

960
01:13:11,330 --> 01:13:14,391
Every mother giving suck shall forget her suckling baby,

961
01:13:14,812 --> 01:13:21,244
and every pregnant female she'll drop her load, thou shall see mankind as in a drunken riot,

962
01:13:22,094 --> 01:13:25,189
yet not drunk, but dreadful would be the Wrath of Allah,

963
01:13:28,779 --> 01:13:31,167
and then compare this to what the Allah says about the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء).

964
01:13:31,247 --> 01:13:34,446
وَلا تَحسَبَنَّ الَّذينَ قُتِلوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ أَمواتًا ۚ

965
01:13:34,654 --> 01:13:36,512
بَل أَحياءٌ عِندَ رَبِّهِم يُرزَقونَ۞

966
01:13:37,075 --> 01:13:39,315
فَرِحينَ بِما آتاهُمُ اللَّهُ مِن فَضلِهِ

967
01:13:39,736 --> 01:13:44,948
 وَيَستَبشِرونَ بِالَّذينَ لَم يَلحَقوا بِهِم مِن خَلفِهِم أَلّا خَوفٌ عَلَيهِم وَلا هُم يَحزَنونَ۞

968
01:13:46,577 --> 01:13:50,659
Think not of those who are slain in the Allah’s way and dead,

969
01:13:51,179 --> 01:13:55,759
Nay they live, finding their sustenance in the presence of their Lord.

970
01:13:56,297 --> 01:13:59,026
They rejoice in the bounty provided by Allah

971
01:13:59,436 --> 01:14:04,340
and with regard to those left behind, who have not yet joined them in their bliss.

972
01:14:04,720 --> 01:14:11,158
The martyrs glory in the fact that on them has no fear, nor have they cause to grief,

973
01:14:11,757 --> 01:14:14,814
and this is Al-Imran(ألعمران) Verse 169 and 170.

974
01:14:15,510 --> 01:14:19,232
These martyrs are saved from the greatest fears and their abode is paradise.

975
01:14:19,812 --> 01:14:22,433
Their souls are in the insides of green birds.

976
01:14:23,870 --> 01:14:26,465
I guess some of you are tired so might need to take a break.

